JEE-2022-ONLINE-PHY-082.s:
$
\frac{\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{X}}}{\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{Y}}}=\frac{\ell_{\mathrm{X}}}{\ell_{\mathrm{Y}}}
$
When wire is stretched to double of its length, then resistance becomes 4 times
$
\begin{aligned}
&amp;\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{W}}=4 \mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{X}}=2 \mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{Y}} \\\\
&amp;\frac{\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{X}}}{\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{Y}}}=\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}
$
So. $\frac{\ell_{\mathrm{x}}}{\ell_{\mathrm{y}}}=\frac{1}{2}$

